# Apex lanes
The contract is skill `steward` §Lane (`.claude/skills/steward/SKILL.md`; one session, one issue, one PR); this rule only points at it.
- Work comes from a `ready` issue. A Cursor agent does not post the claim comment (`steward/references/vendors.md`).
- Draft PR on `cursor/<topic>-<hash>` into `claude/f1-game-project-26h3ng`, template body, and a ```handoff
  block (branch, head, owner, lane, verified, not-run, next) kept current. Put `lane:cursor` in `next:`. A
  Cursor agent cannot set labels (`steward/references/vendors.md`).
- Comments on the issue or PR are the only messages; the PR is the report. No bus, no watcher lane, no
  second hand-off format.
- Subsystem boundaries follow the issue's `area:*` label: UI chrome (menus, HUD, garage sheets) vs car meshes and
  liveries vs track scenery vs perf. A path in an OPEN PR's diff belongs to that PR (AGENTS.md §Git branch & deploy).
- GitHub lands PRs (`land` label, `land.yml`); no agent merges or arms. Model:
  `composer-2.5` routine; Grok 7 hard only (slug at launch); never `default`/Auto.
